From 0c896aa2896f321b0ffb941ad406541a11e12fff Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 04:51:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): judge a document with no machine against the
 default machine's limits

The program gate read only a mounted machine. A document with no mount
posts with the default machine file, but its spindle range and axis feed
rates were not judged: a 7000 mm/min feed above the default 5000 posted,
and a speed above 12000 rpm was refused only by an engine warning that
named no operation.

The gate now judges the ops of each mount with no machine against the
limits the default file states (spindle range, X/Y/Z feed rates), and
refuses by the operation and the limit. A mounted machine is judged by
its own file only, as before.

Fixes #2321

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
